WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.210
Week 22: Double Pronouns, Se, and Reference. report accidental events give concise instructions maintain reference across sentences

2
00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:15.647
Cultural lens. How accidental-se constructions frame agency and responsibility.

3
00:00:15.647 --> 00:00:27.739
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:27.739 --> 00:00:39.533
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:48.575
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:48.575 --> 00:01:14.705
Model language. Se me perdieron las llaves. — I lost my keys. El informe se lo mandé a Clara. — I sent the report to Clara. A ellos se les olvidó la cita. — They forgot the appointment. Explícaselo antes de la reunión. — Explain it to him or her before the meeting. No se nos cayó el equipo; falló el soporte. — We did not drop the equipment; the support failed.

7
00:01:14.705 --> 00:01:24.603
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
